1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,868
Welcome to the official demonstration of the Pharos On-Chain Alert Bot, built for the Pharos Agent Arena.

2
00:00:06,868 --> 00:00:19,330
This autonomous monitoring agent tracks live blockchain events on the Pharos Atlantic Testnet, verifies configurable conditions, and delivers real-time notifications with zero repeat spam.

3
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:34,286
Here on the production dashboard, we see live network telemetry connected to Atlantic Testnet at Chain ID 688689, with continuous block tracking and active deduplication safeguards.

4
00:00:34,286 --> 00:00:45,314
First, we activate a pre-configured alert condition: the Atlantic USDC Whale Alert, monitoring Test USDC transfers exceeding fifty dollars.

5
00:00:45,314 --> 00:00:57,476
Next, we create a custom alert condition through the configuration modal, specifying an Atlantic Micro-Activity Sentinel tracking transfers of zero point zero zero one USDC.

6
00:00:57,476 --> 00:01:08,109
Now, let's trigger a live on-chain block scan. The scanner evaluates recent Atlantic Testnet blocks directly against the official DP Labs RPC.

7
00:01:08,109 --> 00:01:17,501
The scan audit report appears instantly, confirming the exact block range, evaluated logs, and serverless execution latency.

8
00:01:17,501 --> 00:01:32,038
Crucially, our system enforces a deterministic deduplication invariant. When a consecutive scan executes over the same blocks, existing events are recognized and deduplicated, preventing any duplicate spam.

9
00:01:32,038 --> 00:01:42,841
Every detected alert includes full event context: transaction activity, formatted values, block numbers, and verified clickable PharosScan explorer links.

10
00:01:42,841 --> 00:01:56,213
With a zero-cost serverless architecture, comprehensive test coverage, and transparent execution, the Pharos On-Chain Alert Bot delivers enterprise-grade blockchain monitoring. Thank you.
